        "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061xarccot{x}^{3}.$",
        "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of $\\text{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccotx)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, the formula above and the chain rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061xarccot{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot{x}^{3})+arccot{x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x\\cdot (-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{1+{({x}^{3})}^{2}})+arccot{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{arccot{x}^{3}}{x}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}{1+{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
